<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sfatul Țării</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Council of the Country</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sfatul Țării, the 'Council of the Country', was the regional assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> formed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution of 1917</a> and meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chisinau">Chișinău</a>. On 2 December 1917 it proclaimed the Moldavian Democratic Republic. With Romanian troops in the country, it voted on 9 April 1918 (27 March Old Style) for union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, and dissolved itself later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sfatul-tarii.jpg" alt="Sfatul Țării" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex:D · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sfatul_Tarii.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
